<DarkPage title="About me" description="Behavioural ecologist turned machine-learning engineer.">
  <h1>Behavioural ecologist, turned ML engineer.</h1>

  <p>
    I hold a PhD in behavioural ecology (James Cook University; published in
    <em>Animal Behaviour</em>). For years I scored fish behaviour by hand — line
    crossings, feeding strikes, chases — frame by frame. AquaMind is the pipeline
    that does that automatically.
  </p>

  <p>
    The behavioural-ecologist × ML-engineer combination is the point: I know what
    the behaviours mean and how they are measured in the field, not just how to
    detect a moving blob.
  </p>

  <h2>Background</h2>
  <ul>
    <li>PhD, behavioural ecology — James Cook University</li>
    <li>Postgraduate AI — Erasmus Hogeschool Brussels</li>
    <li>PCAP-certified Python programmer</li>
  </ul>

  <h2>Tech</h2>
  <p>
    Python · PyTorch (CNN, LSTM, transfer learning) · OpenCV · MySQL ·
    NumPy / Pandas · scikit-learn · MLflow · DVC · Docker · FastAPI
  </p>
</DarkPage>
